<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Columbia/HCA downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Columbia/HCA downgraded.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Stephens Inc analyst Nancy Weaver said in a research note that she lowered her recommendation on Columbia/HCA Healthcare Corp to buy from strong buy on a valuation basis.</p>
<p>-- Shares rose 1/4 to 40-1/8 in early NYSE trade.  </p>
<p>-- &quot;We continue to believe that Columbia will have little difficulty in maintaining its targeted 15 percent earnings growth rate in spite of various investors' concerns. We are fine-tuning our 1997 EPS estimate by $0.01 from $2.58 to $2.57,&quot; the research note said.</p>
<p>-- The 1996 estimate is $2.22 per share.</p>
<p>-- Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1730</p>
</text>
